      "title": "As the Coalition stares down One Nation in NSW, a new threat is rising: the teals",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/21/coalition-one-nation-teals-new-threat-sydney",
      "description": "<p>The opposition’s struggle is creating an opportunity for progressive independents who are boosted by shrewd political operator Chris Minns</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The New South Wales Coalition is facing a renewed threat to its heartland seats on Sydney’s north shore.</p><p>This time, the threat is from independent candidates – and they’re backed by the same community activists who put a swathe of teal independents into federal parliament.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/21/coalition-one-nation-teals-new-threat-sydney\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-20T14:00:32"
    },
    {
      "title": "Vape users hospitalised after losing consciousness, prompting public health warning in New South Wales",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/20/vape-users-hospitalised-after-losing-consciousness-prompting-public-health-warning-in-new-south-wales",
      "description": "<p>Testing confirms presence of etomidate, a strong and fast-acting sedative used as a general anaesthetic overseas but not registered for medical use in Australia</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Three people who lost consciousness and were hospitalised in New South Wales after using certain vapes have tested positive for the unregulated anaesthetic agent etomidate, health officials said.</p><p>NSW health on Friday issued a public warning about vape liquids containing etomidate, a strong and fast-acting sedative used as a general anaesthetic overseas but not registered for medical use in Australia.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/20/vape-users-hospitalised-after-losing-consciousness-prompting-public-health-warning-in-new-south-wales\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-20T07:17:01"
    },
    {
      "title": "Baby born with heart abnormalities ‘didn’t have a chance’ after non-medical free birth, NSW inquest hears",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/20/routine-checks-may-have-saved-babies-lives-freebirth-inquest-nsw-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Inquest into the deaths of four babies after free and home births hears routine checks and follow-up may have saved their lives</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Four babies who died in New South Wales – three after free births and one after a home birth – might have survived if they had had routine checks and follow-up , a coronial inquest has heard.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/18/byron-bay-doula-left-newborn-to-inflate-jumping-castle-freebirth-inquest-ntwnfb\">Baby DH</a>, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/17/nsw-inquest-free-birth-keeper-baby-death-ntwnfb\">Baby D</a>, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/16/nsw-inquest-four-babies-freebirth-home-birth-northern-rivers-ntwnfb\">Baby R</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/19/mother-whose-twin-baby-died-was-determined-to-have-home-birth-despite-expert-advice-nsw-inquest-hears-ntwnfb\">Baby B</a> died in the state’s northern rivers region between 2022 and 2024.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/20/routine-checks-may-have-saved-babies-lives-freebirth-inquest-nsw-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-20T06:51:54"
    },
    {
      "title": "Kellie Sloane says she’s ‘pretty sure’ NSW Liberals exodus is over after Mark Speakman resigns",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/19/mark-speakman-resigns-and-says-liberals-face-existential-threat-as-nsw-exodus-continues",
      "description": "<p>Former opposition leader warns party against being ‘One Nation lite’ as he becomes eighth out of 24 Liberal MPs not to recontest seat in March</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The New South Wales opposition leader, Kellie Sloane, says she is “pretty sure” the exodus of Liberals before the March state election has finished, after Mark Speakman became the eighth MP to decide not to recontest their lower house seats.</p><p>In a late-night speech on Thursday, the final sitting day of NSW’s legislative assembly before the vote, Speakman said he would not run again in his south Sydney seat of Cronulla, which he has held since 2011.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/19/mark-speakman-resigns-and-says-liberals-face-existential-threat-as-nsw-exodus-continues\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-20T05:02:16"
    },
    {
      "title": "Beau Lamarre-Condon’s explanations of body disposal ‘ring hollow’, court hears",
