      "description": "<p>Former police officer has pleaded not guilty to murdering Jesse Baird and Luke Davies in Paddington in February 2024</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Beau Lamarre-Condon knew he had murdered two men and his attempts to explain the disposal of their bodies “ring completely hollow”, a court has heard.</p><p>Lamarre-Condon is accused of fatally shooting Jesse Baird and his new partner, Luke Davies, with his police service weapon in Baird’s Paddington home in Sydney on 19 February 2024.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/20/beau-lamarre-condons-attempts-to-explain-disposal-alleged-victims-bodies-ring-hollow-court-hears-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
